WR_xPu-RELk0R8_UZRnrDPJIw-VZASFsq\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Investigating Flyway-core version skew**\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Documenting metadata ownership and manual intervention**\"}]}"}, {"type": "text", "text": "### Human intervention needed\n\nThe automated job failed in `explore/generate_tests()` while trying to create a test for the reporter-requested reflection access to `PrepareScriptFilenameConfigurationExtension.getUndoFilename()`.\n\nPreserved work: https://github.com/oracle/graalvm-reachability-metadata/tree/ai%2Fkimeta%2Fhuman-intervention%2Fissue-10323-fails-native-image-run-org.flywaydb-flyway-database-postgresql-11.12.0-b78f7bc4\n\nEvidence:\n- `fixTestNativeImageRun` completed successfully and generated metadata, so the initial metadata-repair stage was not the terminal failure.\n- The dynamic-access report completed successfully and covered all 6 calls in `PostgreSQLCopyParsedStatement`, but it did not represent the reported access in the `flyway-core` class.\n- All three generation attempts proposed configuring `flyway.prepare.undoFilename`, but each transcript says tests were not run. No test changes survived: metrics record 3 iterations, 0 generated LOC, and identical starting/ending commits.\n- The setup preflight was also degraded after classifying the existing `docker run` test setup as unsafe, although setup and the initial fix still completed.\n\nInspect:\n- `human-intervention-logs/org.flywaydb:flyway-database-postgresql:11.12.0/issue-requested-metadata/pi.log`\n- `human-intervention-logs/org.flywaydb:flyway-database-postgresql:11.12.0/issue-requested-metadata/pi-generation-2026-10-06T23-15-27-948217Z.log`\n- `human-intervention-logs/org.flywaydb:flyway-database-postgresql:11.12.0/native-image-run-fix/fixTestNativeImageRun-2026-10-06T23-06-18-015071Z.log`\n- `human-intervention-logs/org.flywaydb:flyway-database-postgresql:11.12.0/dynamic-access-report/generateDynamicAccessCoverageReport-2026-10-06T23-10-09-672665Z.log`\n\nManual next steps:\n1. Reproduce the issue’s clean native test command for version `11.12.0` and confirm the `getUndoFilename()` failure.\n2. Add a public-API test that exercises `flyway.prepare.undoFilename`, remains compatible with the shared `11.8.1` test project, and run it on both JVM and Native Image.\n3. Regenerate and validate metadata, confirming whether the reflection entry belongs to `flyway-core` rather than `flyway-database-postgresql`.", "textSignature": "{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_02bcdb7b051df832016ac581ef85d487d0be2dbbe5017d04a3\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}], "api": "openai-codex-responses", "provider": "openai-codex", "model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "usage": {"input": 15140, "output": 1485, "cacheRead": 152320, "cacheWrite": 0, "reasoning": 925, "totalTokens": 168945, "cost": {"input": 0.060559999999999996, "output": 0.0297, "cacheRead": 0.060928, "cacheWrite": 0, "total": 0.151188}}, "stopReason": "stop", "timestamp": 1791328731418, "responseId": "resp_02bcdb7b051df832016ac581dc051487d0a45ae30f25739c7e", "rawStopReason": "completed"}}
